{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1098494-need-a-fifth-player-for-a-new-chronicle","id":1098494,"title":"Need a fifth player for a new Chronicle.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-30T11:32:39-07:00","id":1098494,"title":"Need a fifth player for a new Chronicle.","content":"I'm putting together a group to play Werewolf on Roll20 but one of the players had to drop out because his schedule changed, so I thought I'd ask the people here.<br /> <br /> Chronicle Information:<br /> <br /> - I'm using the Revised edition corebook, but only because I don't have the 20th-anniversary book. We can work out any issues that version differences might cause.<br /> <br /> - It's set in Vancouver, British Columbia during the early 1990's, for those that don't know; Vancouver contains a very powerful caern of cooperation known as The Great Caern where all 13 tribes (the Stargazers haven't left yet) work together and have a representative on the Council that makes all the big decisions. There's also a truce between the Garou and the Vampires that live in the city; as long as they don't kill anyone and use their business connections to reduce the amount of logging and such in the province, then the werewolves won't attack them or interfere with them.<br /> <br /> - Garou only, no other Changing Breeds. I would like a Ragabash character since the other four auspices have been filled, but aside from that no restrictions on what kind of character you can play, aside from having some reason to be joining a pack. You could have a character that comes from anywhere in the world and I would let you play them as long as they fit the previous conditions. I'm going to run a Prelude session at some point before the Chronicle begins.<br /> <br /> - We will be playing on the Roll20 website, which if you don't know is a tabletop game simulator. It's free and has a bunch of nifty tools like character sheets and virtual dice rollers. In addition, we will be using Discord for voice chat which is also free, and in my opinion, better than Skype.<br /> <br /> - Games will be held on Wednesdays, starting at 6:30 pm Atlantic Time, and will last for three to five hours, never much longer than that.<br /> <br /> - I would hope this goes without saying, but just so we're clear: I expect respect for both myself and the other players. Games like this do not work out when the players can't get along.<br /> <br /> - In a similar vein, I'm not a Werewolf: the Apocalypse expert; I have a lot of books but haven't read most of them. So if I get some setting stuff wrong I would prefer to prefer to be politely corrected than any other possible reaction. I'm already using a few house rules because they make more sense to me, but we can discuss it if it comes up.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry to say I will only be accepting one person, I don't think I could handle a huge group. You can respond on this Topic or send me a Private Message.<br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13528,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13528-lordpyrus25","user":"LordPyrus25","date":". 05-30-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13528-lordpyrus25","name":"LordPyrus25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}